<hr />
<h2>One Principle: Localization Must Come First</h2>
<p>The core lesson isn't about any single tactic—it's about mindset. Localization is often treated as something to optimize "after launch." But when it's not baked in from account setup through creative production, every dollar spent funds the wrong strategy.</p>
<p>Southeast Asia and Latin America may seem like low-barrier entry points, but each market has unique cultural rhythms and spending habits. Investing upfront in localization costs far less than retesting, re-opening accounts, and re-depositing budget after failures.</p>
